	This code compiles under Borland C++ v3.1.  It works only for DOS,
not Windows.

	This is some sample code to get the PGSI working in AGE request
mode.  It simply prints the PGSI data to the screen in an infinite loop
after it finishes initializing.  It also drives the SEGA glasses, making
them switch from left to right in the same infinite loop.

	Some of the initialization code is a little messy with delays and
such due to my lack of understanding of the initial state of the glove and
pgsi upon power-up.

